From 7cde3cca60d60bc2c461b63dbcc929351617b170 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: keep the sound on an output that hades-keep-outputs
 keeps on

The windowing system keeps on the outputs that hades-keep-outputs
names (CDRMUtils::KeepsOutputOn()), whatever the expert setting "Keep
the display of the audio output on" (audiooutput.hadeslightforsound)
says. The audio engine only looked at the setting: with it off, the
sound of an output whose display is not the one in use went to the
output of the display in use (INTERNAL::OutputForDisplayInUse()), as if
that output were off.

Issue #24 (2026-11-13): an AV receiver on the HDMI port of the board (an
LSPCON, DP-1 of i915), named in hades-keep-outputs, and the TV on an RTX
3050 for the picture. The log says "DP-1 stay(s) on as it was, for its
sound (hades-keep-outputs)" and, the same second, that the sound goes
to the TV because "Keep the display of the audio output on" is off.

An output that the file keeps on now counts as one that the setting
keeps on (DisplaysFor(), KeptOnByUser()). The kernel has no link from a
PCM to a connector, so it is matched as the windowing system matches
the sound in use (KEEP_OUTPUTS::OutputsForSound()): the sound card to
its graphics device by the PCI bus (CardOfDevice()), and the display of
the PCM, by its ELD, to the display of an output that the file keeps
on, by its EDID (SameDisplay()). The outputs are read from
/sys/class/drm, whose names the file uses, so the graphics devices that
Kodi does not draw on count too (ActiveAEKeptOutputs.h). Where that is
not certain (no display or no card known, no such output), the setting
decides as before. Nothing is read where the file keeps nothing. The
decision is logged at INFO once for each change, for each output.

The windowing system says the same: with the setting off, an output
that the file keeps on stays in the decision of OutputsForSound() with
the sound that goes to it, and the log no longer says that it "is not
kept on" for that sound.

Tests: TestActiveAEKeptOutputs (the outputs of the PC of #24 as a
/sys/class/drm in a temporary folder, the file with an output name, a
name on one card, "*", nothing; and OutputsForSound() with and without
the file), 6 pass; TestActiveAEFollowDisplay, 32 pass; six mutants of
the change are caught.
